# What Does Meta Use?

Meta doesn't publicly disclose a universal semantic chunking model.

Internally they often build custom embedding systems.

Large companies frequently use:

```text
Fine-tuned embedding model
```

instead of off-the-shelf MiniLM.

---

# What Does Microsoft Use?

For enterprise search and Copilot-related systems Microsoft commonly uses embedding models from Azure/OpenAI ecosystems rather than MiniLM.

---

# What Does Google Use?

Google generally uses proprietary embedding models from Gemini infrastructure.

Again:

```text
Semantic chunking
Retrieval
Ranking
```

often share the same embedding space.

---

# A Common Misconception

Many people think:

```text
Chunking Model = Retrieval Model
```

must always be identical.

Not necessarily.

You could do:

```text
MiniLM
     ↓
Semantic Chunking

OpenAI Embeddings
     ↓
Retrieval
```

and it will work.

But quality is often better when both use the same embedding family.

---

