# If You Were Building Something Like ChatGPT/OpenClaw

I would not use MiniLM.

I would use:

```text
bge-m3
```

or

```text
text-embedding-3-large
```

for:

* semantic chunking
* retrieval
* reranking pipeline

because retrieval quality becomes much more important than the small savings from MiniLM.

---

So the code you were shown:

```python
HuggingFaceEmbeddings(
    model_name="sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"
)
```

is **not just a toy example**. It is genuinely used in many real production systems. However, among modern high-quality RAG systems in 2025–2026, it is increasingly common to use stronger embedding models such as **BGE**, **E5**, **Nomic**, **Snowflake Arctic**, **Voyage**, or **OpenAI text-embedding-3-large**, depending on cost, latency, and quality requirements.
